## Comparative protein structure analysis with PCA

We start with a database id "1ake_A"

```{r}
library(bio3d)
aa <- get.seq("1ake_A")
aa
```

> Q10. Which of the packages above is found only on BioConductor and not CRAN? 

msa

> Q12. True or False? Functions from the pak package can be used to install packages from GitHub and BitBucket? 

TRUE

> Q13. How many amino acids are in this sequence, i.e. how long is this sequence? 

214

```{r}
b <- blast.pdb(aa)
b
```

To see a bit:
```{r}
head( b$hit.tbl )
```


```{r}
hits <- plot(b)
```

```{r}
head(hits$pdb.id)
```

Now we can download these "top hits" these will all be ADK structures in the PDB database.

```{r}
hits <- NULL
hits$pdb.id <- c('1AKE_A','6S36_A','6RZE_A','3HPR_A','1E4V_A','5EJE_A','1E4Y_A','3X2S_A','6HAP_A','6HAM_A','4K46_A','3GMT_A','4PZL_A')
files <- get.pdb(hits$pdb.id, path="pdbs", split=TRUE, gzip=TRUE)
```

We need one package from BioConductor. To set this up we need to first install a package called **BiocManager** from CRAN.

Now we can use the `install()` function from this package like this: 
`BiocManager::install("msa")`

```{r}
pdbs <- pdbaln(files, fit = TRUE, exefile="msa")
```

Let's have a peek at our structures after "fitting" or superposing:

```{r}
library(bio3dview)

#view.pdbs(pdbs)
```

```{r}
#view.pdbs(pdbs, colorScheme = "residue")
```

```{r}
ids <- basename.pdb(pdbs$id)

anno <- pdb.annotate(ids)
unique(anno$source)
```

```{r}
anno
```

We can run functions like `rmsd()`, or `rmsf()` and the best `pca()`

```{r}
pc.xray <- pca(pdbs)
plot(pc.xray)
```

```{r}
rd <- rmsd(pdbs)
hc.rd <- hclust(dist(rd))
grps.rd <- cutree(hc.rd, k=3)

plot(pc.xray, 1:2, col="grey50", bg=grps.rd, pch=21, cex=1)
```

Finally lets make a little movie of the major 
"motion" of structural difference in the dataset - we call this a "trajectory"

```{r}
pc1 <- mktrj(pc.xray, pc=1, file="pc_1.pdb")
```

```{r}
library(ggplot2)
library(ggrepel)

df <- data.frame(PC1=pc.xray$z[,1], 
                 PC2=pc.xray$z[,2], 
                 col=as.factor(grps.rd),
                 ids=ids)

p <- ggplot(df) + 
  aes(PC1, PC2, col=col, label=ids) +
  geom_point(size=2) +
  geom_text_repel(max.overlaps = 20) +
  theme(legend.position = "none")
p

```

## Normal Mode analysis

```{r}
modes <- nma(pdbs)
plot(modes, pdbs, col=grps.rd)
```




